          "english_quote": "so that none of those who search for the truth ungratefully may find it, but instead may find what he wants",
          "issue": "The draft attaches τὸ ἀληθές to ζητούντων and supplies an understood object for εὕρῃ. This is grammatically defensible, but the more direct attachment makes 'the truth' the object of 'find,' particularly because ἀλλ’ ὃ βούλεται supplies the contrasting object of finding. The difference matters: the draft explicitly characterizes these people as searching for truth, whereas the alternative leaves their search’s object unspecified. The notes discuss gratitude terminology but not this attachment choice.",
